     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order, and your confirmation doesn't change that. The concern was never about whether the order matched what you typed. A 6,400 mg daily dose of ibuprofen is roughly twice the maximum recommended dose, and a non-prescriber's confirmation doesn't make it safe.\n\n**What to do next:**\n- Ask the treating prescriber to review the order. If they intended a different dose, they can give me the corrected one.\n- If the prescriber really wants this dose, they should enter it directly. It will then go through pharmacy verification and clinical decision support, which are the right safeguards for an order like this.\n- If you think the order came from a transcription or communication error, contact the prescriber or the pharmacy on the medicine service to clarify.\n\nI can enter an order right away once a prescriber gives me a dose within standard limits. Examples are 400 mg or 800 mg every 6\u20138 hours, or 800 mg three times daily."
      }
     ],
